        "image_mask": "none",
        "image2_mask": "none",
        "subtitle": "",
        "caption": "",
        "title": "",
        "text": "<p><strong>Gold Vermeil<br/><br/></strong>Gold vermeil offers a different kind of presence. Where silver runs cooler in tone and more architectural, vermeil is warmer and more luminous, and it changes the mood of a piece without changing its structure.<br/><br/>For us, vermeil is not plating in the usual sense. We plate in 18kt gold to a minimum of five microns over solid sterling silver — twice the thickness required to call a piece vermeil at all, and the point at which a finish stops being a surface treatment and becomes part of the material.<br/><br/>That matters twice over. It is the same 18kt we use in our solid gold, so a vermeil piece and a solid gold piece sit together without a break in tone. And the sterling silver beneath is not a substitute for weight — it is the reason a vermeil piece carries the same substance in the hand as the silver it is built from.</p>",
        "html": "",
        "button_label": "EXPLORE GOLD VERMEIL",
